  "model": "s2.1-pro-free",
  "text": "The gathering began after the last boat returned and Mara had helped its passengers ashore. She crossed to the garden with her work finished. This time, she could read The Torn Wing there herself.\n\nThese are my two reusable footbridge sections. Six posts and two ropes are beside them. The posts support the ropes along the two sides of the walkway. Keep the middle clear for walking. —Grandma\n\nPip crossed the river with a way back behind him. In the garden, he and Grandma planted the seed she had given him. He had kept his promise. A lantern-flower grew where they had worked together.\n\nMara was still working at the dock when the gathering began. With her permission, Pip read The Torn Wing from her page. Her story reached the garden while she stayed with the passengers.\n\nOn his last visit, Pip had held out his palm while Grandma tipped a lantern seed into it. It was smaller than he had expected. He could close his hand around it without making a fist.\n\nThe two older stories already belong to the garden. The waiting flowers will keep the new stories people share. You can inspect any flower; there is no collection total to complete.\n\nKeep the boat’s route clear. When you reach the garden, prepare our planting spot with me, place the seed and cover it with soil. The bridge stays in place so everyone can return.\n\nRainwater can carry dirt through the roof. I cannot use flour that got wet that way. Once we know this flour stayed dry, we can measure it and add clean water for the dough.\n\nUse Move earlier and Move later, or drag a card by its handle. You can also focus a handle and use the up and down arrow keys. New moments join the end of your arrangement.",
  "textSha256": "e4d2d2188ea533a2a57ca0d7c97cd98e9b243d3fae7d26d7e03d5a7a1099bc8e",
